From: shiro <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] threads-watcher: remove dead code after DB-source-of-truth migration

After watcher.py was rewritten to use SQLite (db.py) as the source of truth,
the following state.json-era helpers became unreachable:

  - STATE_FILE constant
  - _load_state()
  - _save_state()
  - _write_web_snapshot()  (old `post_ids` shape, superseded by `_write_web_snapshot_from_db`)
  - _check_handle()        (superseded by inline run_once)

Verified unreferenced via grep across the entire project. All 34 pytest
cases still pass after removal:
  - tests/test_db.py: 9 passed
  - tests/test_health.py: 10 passed
  - tests/test_extract_post_ids.py: 11 passed
  - tests/test_autoincrement_gap.py: 4 passed
And the CLI smoke test `python watcher.py --health-check` returns exit 0
unchanged.

Apply to any tree where the dead code is still present:
  git apply qa-reports/threads-watcher-dead-code-removal-2026-05-17.patch

No external publishing. push deferred to Yakon approval.

